 New regression assertions cover the default semantic zoom band, a 130 px minimum default Object screen width, and a maximum 3.2 layout aspect ratio across all four fixtures. The measured wrapped layouts were Small `2480 × 1258`, Medium `4338 × 2945`, Large `9333 × 3580`, and Complex `7385 × 4789`; all existing non-overlap, orthogonality, obstacle, label-point, determinism and incremental-stability checks continued to pass.
 
+## 2026-08-31 multi-select union impact
+
+The Inspect impact read model now generalizes from one root to a selection set, without changing the Semantic Graph boundary, the adapter, validation, cache behavior or the read-only Human Web contract.
+
+- `CanvasInteractionState` carries an ordered `selectedObjectIds` set. Plain click selects one object; Ctrl/Cmd+click toggles objects; Shift+drag draws the React Flow marquee. React Flow remains the source of truth for the selection set through `onSelectionChange`; the canvas only mirrors it and keeps Focus/Trace contracts untouched.
+- `deriveImpact` accepts multiple roots and computes the union: per-root BFS with minimum hop depth across roots, merged role per object (`upstream` / `downstream` / `both`), and per-relationship roles. Selected roots stay part of the selection, never the impacted set, even when another root reaches them.
+- Shared impact is explicit: `contributorCount` records how many selected roots reach each impacted object, and objects with two or more contributors are exposed as `sharedObjectIds`. Shared objects render an amber `⇄ n` chip and border; the Inspector aggregate panel lists counts (selected, upstream, downstream, shared) plus the full impacted object list sorted shared-first, with one-click drill-down to any listed object. Clearing the selection returns the Inspector to its idle state.
+- Camera contracts are preserved: multi-selection frames the union of selected roots and their impact in Browse/Inspect; Focus and Trace framing and emphasis are unchanged.
+- Group drags persist every selected object's device-local position and only invalidate routes that touch moved objects; `deleteKeyCode` is disabled so Backspace can never delete view nodes.
+- Regression coverage lives in `tests/canvas-impact.test.mjs` (union/shared semantics, projection mapping, aggregate binding, idle reset, single-select invariants, Focus/Trace invariance, Small 15/20 and Medium 40/70 fixture scales, and a production-shaped Registry adapter bundle). Real-browser evidence for Ctrl+click, marquee, Focus/Trace invariance, idle reset, Medium fixture and the production `ecp-core` Registry project is captured under `evidence/multi-select-*.png` via `scripts/capture-multi-select-evidence.mjs`.
+
